## The permission

> If you modify this Program, or any covered work, by linking or
> combining it with a **Camera Support Library** (or a modified version
> of such a library), the licensors of this Program grant you additional
> permission to convey the resulting work. Corresponding Source for a
> non-source form of such a combination shall include the source code
> for the parts of this Program used in that combination, but need not
> include the source of the Camera Support Library itself.

A **Camera Support Library** means any library, driver, runtime or
software development kit whose purpose is to operate imaging hardware or
the equipment it is attached to, including but not limited to camera
manufacturers' SDKs, machine-vision and photographic-tethering
libraries, and motorised stage, filter-wheel and illumination control
libraries — together with any bindings distributed with them for the
purpose of using them.

This permission applies whether the library is linked, loaded at run
time, or invoked through a binding, and whether or not its own licence
is compatible with the GNU General Public License.

## Scope

This permission grants no rights in the hardware libraries themselves.
Their own licences are unaffected, and nothing here permits you to
redistribute them. darlaston does not bundle any of them.

It applies only to libraries whose purpose is operating imaging
hardware. It does not permit linking darlaston with proprietary software
for any other purpose.

